87. SERVICE TRANSACTION POLICY
Application services determine transaction boundaries.
A service operation that changes authoritative project state must execute through the Unit of Work.
Read-only operations may use controlled read sessions.
Long-running computation must not hold a PostgreSQL transaction open unnecessarily.

88. LONG-RUNNING OPERATIONS
The following shall be asynchronous:
large geometry generation
full compliance validation
large drawing sets
document package generation
complex Aria processing
The HTTP API returns:
job_id
status
rather than holding the request open.

89. COMMAND / JOB DISTINCTION
A command represents:
WHAT SHOULD HAPPEN
A job represents:
WORK REQUIRED TO COMPLETE IT
These concepts remain separate.
Example:
GenerateDrawingsCommand
        ↓
DrawingGenerationJob
        ↓
DrawingService

90. EVENT / JOB DISTINCTION
An event represents:
WHAT HAS HAPPENED
A job represents:
WHAT MUST BE DONE
Therefore:
ModelChanged
is an event.
GenerateAffectedDrawings
is a job.

91. RECONSTRUCTION REQUIREMENT
The service layer must preserve the v0.1 reconstruction guarantee.
